# LibreWolf no-suggest.patch  (Android)
# Owner: LW-M4-11 ("Disable search suggestions and the top-sites contile feed")
#
# Upstream files touched
# -----------------------
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/HomeActivity.kt
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/HomeSettingsFragment.kt
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/xml/home_preferences.xml
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/SettingsTest.kt
#
# All line numbers below are from the ESR tree (firefox-153.0esr, ./version.android),
# AFTER the patches listed before this one in assets/patches/android.txt.
#
#
# What desktop does, and what Android did instead
# ------------------------------------------------
# Desktop LibreWolf ships browser.search.suggest.enabled=false (settings/common.cfg)
# and has no sponsored new-tab tiles. Fenix does not read that pref: the toolbar
# is a Kotlin/Compose view and the suggestion fetch is Fenix's own
# SearchSuggestionProvider (android-components feature-awesomebar), gated by
# Settings.shouldShowSearchSuggestions, whose default was `true`
# (Settings.kt:1628-1631). So on a stock build every keystroke in the toolbar
# went to the engine's suggestion endpoint before Enter, and a second provider
# (TrendingSearchProvider, Settings.trendingSearchSuggestionsEnabled, default
# `true` at :1650-1653) fetched the engine's trending list with an EMPTY query
# the moment the toolbar was focused.
#
# Sponsored tiles ("Contile") are a separate feed. In 153 there is no
# contile.services.mozilla.com any more -- the feed is the MARS / Mozilla ads
# client and the host is ads.mozilla.org (measured by LW-M4-10, see
# no-onboarding.patch, "The two wrong answers"). It is scheduled from three
# places, all in HomeActivity.kt: a TopSitesRefresher lifecycle observer
# (:595-603, refresh on every resume), ContileTopSitesUpdater.startPeriodicWork()
# (:638-640, WorkManager periodic job) and its stopPeriodicWork() in onDestroy
# (:916). All three were gated on Settings.showContileFeature, a preference
# defaulting to `true` (:2182-2185) with a "Sponsored shortcuts" checkbox in
# Settings > Homepage.
#
#
# What this patch does
# ---------------------
# 1. Search suggestions OFF by default -- a default, not a lock. The two
#    preferences keep their keys and their rows in Settings > Search
#    (SearchEngineFragment.kt:82,92), so the user can turn them on. Acceptance
#    line 3 ("the suggestion setting is still user-toggleable") is why this is
#    `default = false` and not a constant.
#
# 2. Sponsored tiles REMOVED, not switched off. The brief is explicit that a
#    switched-off remote feed is still a code path an upstream default can
#    revive, so:
#      * Settings.showContileFeature becomes a constant `false` getter. There is
#        no preference behind it any more, so no settings write, no Nimbus
#        experiment and no upstream default flip can turn it on. The remaining
#        readers (TopSitesConfigCreator.kt:48, FenixApplication.kt:460,
#        DefaultTopSitesView.kt:22, TermsOfUseDataProvider.kt:74,
#        RecordedNimbusContext.kt:247) all see `false` and need no edit.
#      * The three scheduling call sites in HomeActivity.kt are deleted, so the
#        MARS/MAC providers in Core.kt (marsTopSitesProvider :658,
#        macTopSitesProvider :680, contileTopSitesUpdater :694) are never
#        constructed -- they are `lazyMonitored` and now have no reader.
#      * The "Sponsored shortcuts" checkbox is removed from home_preferences.xml
#        and HomeSettingsFragment.kt, because a visible toggle that does nothing
#        is the over-locking failure LW-M3-04's must-not-lock list exists to
#        prevent.
#    Core.kt itself is deliberately NOT edited: it is shared with
#    fission-isolation.patch and no-nimbus.patch, the providers are inert
#    without a caller, and touching it would only add a shared-file ordering
#    constraint for no runtime difference.
#
# 3. SettingsTest.showSearchSuggestions asserted the upstream default and is
#    flipped to assertFalse. No other unit test pins these defaults: the
#    SearchFragmentStore / FenixSearchMiddleware tests mock Settings, and
#    TopSitesRefresherTest tests the class, which still exists. Nothing in
#    fenix/app/src/test assigns showContileFeature (checked: `grep -rn
#    'showContileFeature\s*='` is empty), so the var->val change compiles.
#
#
# What this patch does NOT cover, with owners
# --------------------------------------------
#   * Firefox Suggest (merino AMP/Wikipedia suggestions): FxSuggestSuggestionProvider
#     is gated on Settings.enableFxSuggest, whose default is the FML value
#     `fx-suggest.enabled = false` (nimbus.fml.yaml:372-384); with no-nimbus.patch
#     the FML default is the only source. Not touched here; LW-M4-03 owns Nimbus.
#   * Pocket / sponsored stories and the merino image CDN: no-onboarding.patch
#     (LW-M4-10).
#   * Search telemetry (search-telemetry-v2 dump, Glean): no-glean.patch (LW-M4-01).
#   * The default engine and partner codes: search-config.patch (LW-M4-06).
#
#
# Ordering
# ---------
# Shares Settings.kt with no-adjust, no-gms, no-onboarding (and the parked
# ubo-preinstall), HomeActivity.kt with no-adjust and no-nimbus, and
# SettingsTest.kt with no-onboarding. Every hunk here is in a region none of
# those patches touch. Order-freedom is MEASURED, not eyeballed: each shared
# file was replayed from the pristine ESR copy through the android.txt sequence
# in list order and once more per partner with this patch moved in front of
# that partner (2026-09-02, both orders, patch exit 0, no .rej, byte-identical
# results -- HomeActivity.kt sha256 cf447dd9..., Settings.kt db719ae5...,
# SettingsTest.kt 0369a329...; the only effect of the order is a line offset).
# Recorded in scripts/check-patch-order.py's REVIEWED_ORDER_FREE. This patch
# is listed after all of them in assets/patches/android.txt.
#
#
# Verification
# -------------
#   ./scripts/android-smoke.sh --check-no-suggest --serial <dev> --apk <apk>
# types into the toolbar and proves nothing leaves before Enter, from the
# emulator's own packet capture -- a pref read would pass on a build that still
# calls the suggestion endpoint, which is the failure this gate exists to catch.
# See docs/android/evidence/lw-m4-11/ for the measured runs.
#
#
# 157 rebase (2026-10-02, Firefox 153.4.0esr -> 157.0)
# -----------------------------------------------------
# Same change, nothing dropped. The line numbers above are 153's. What moved:
#   * Settings.kt was reformatted upstream (ktfmt: `val x by` on its own
#     line, booleanPreference(...) indented below it). The three properties
#     are edited in the new layout; shouldShowSearchSuggestions is now at
#     ~:1742, trendingSearchSuggestionsEnabled ~:1767, showContileFeature
#     ~:2321, and its KDoc became a one-liner that is expanded again here.
#   * HomeActivity.kt: upstream dropped the MARS client; TopSitesRefresher
#     now always takes core.macTopSitesProvider, and contileTopSitesUpdater
#     was renamed core.macTopSitesUpdater. The same three call sites are
#     removed (lifecycle observer, startPeriodicWork, stopPeriodicWork).
#     The TopSitesRefresher import is left in place, as on 153 (kotlinc does
#     not report unused imports), so that this patch does not touch the
#     import block the other HomeActivity patches edit.
#   * Readers of showContileFeature on 157: TopSitesConfigCreator.kt:50,
#     FenixApplication.kt:535 and :1231, DefaultTopSitesView.kt:22,
#     TermsOfUseDataProvider.kt:54, RecordedNimbusContext.kt:250,
#     TopSitesRefresher.kt:43. None assigns it.
#   * Core.kt: topSitesStorage is now always built with macTopSitesProvider,
#     so the provider object is constructed; DefaultTopSitesStorage only
#     queries it when providerConfig.showProviderTopSites is true
#     (DefaultTopSitesStorage.kt:129-136), and both configs set that from
#     showContileFeature, which is constant false. Core.kt is still not
#     edited.
#   * Unit tests on 157 that touch these settings mock them (mockk
#     `every { ... }`, which works on a val), so only SettingsTest needs the
#     flipped assertion.
# Order-freedom vs no-adjust/no-nimbus/no-onboarding/no-gms was not
# re-measured: those patches were still being rebased when this was cut.
#
# 158 rebase (2026-10-04, pre-rebase against Firefox 158.0b3): HomeActivity's
# lifecycle-observer list renamed defaultTopSitesBinding to
# defaultPinnedSitesBinding, the line before the TopSitesRefresher this patch
# removes. Same removal, same comment; the other hunks are the 157 ones at
# their 158 offsets.
